<section id="S6.SS2.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsubsection">6.2.3.  Effect of Course Material Type</h4>

<section id="S6.SS2.SSS3.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Polished transcripts yield the best CPT performancee</h5>

<div id="S6.SS2.SSS3.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.SSS3.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conduct an ablation study to examine the effect of different types of course materials for CPT on model performance. Due to computational constraints, this experiment is limited to the Human–Computer Interaction (HCI) topic. The results are shown in Table <a href="#S6.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ Polished transcripts yield the best CPT performancee ‣ 6.2.3. Effect of Course Material Type ‣ 6.2. LLM Performance with CPT ‣ 6. Results and Discussion ‣ From Slides to Chatbots: Enhancing Large Language Models with University Course Materials" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>. We observe the same pattern: CPT in general performs worse than RAG. Among the CPT configurations, the best results are achieved when using polished transcripts. This outcome is expected, as the polished transcripts more closely resemble the natural text that LLMs are typically trained on.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.T9" class="ltx_table">
<table id="S6.T9.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S6.T9.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T9.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;" colspan="4"><span id="S6.T9.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">LLaMA 3.1</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S6.T9.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T9.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"></th>
<td id="S6.T9.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S6.T9.2.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">HCI</span></td>
<td id="S6.T9.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S6.T9.2.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">HCI</span></td>
<td id="S6.T9.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"></td></tr>
